From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:56:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose current_text_len on TreeBuilder for source-range
 recording

Embedders need to know where each pushed text chunk lands in the
final layout string, for example to record per-text-node ranges for
painting DOM selections. Reports committed + pending length: pending
collapsible whitespace counts as the single space it collapses to,
so a chunk's range ends after its trailing space whenever more
content follows.
---
 src/builder.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/builder.rs b/src/builder.rs
index b45d6b9..c00326c 100644
--- a/src/builder.rs
+++ b/src/builder.rs
@@ -296,6 +296,15 @@ impl<'b, B: Brush> TreeBuilder<'b, B> {
         self.lcx.tree_style_builder.has_pending_whitespace()
     }

+    // Current length of the layout text (committed plus
+    // pending), measured around push_text to record source ranges.
+    // Pending collapsible whitespace collapses to at most one space,
+    // so it counts as one: the range of the text that pushed it ends
+    // after it, as it will if more content follows.
+    pub fn current_text_len(&self) -> usize {
+        self.text().len() + usize::from(self.has_pending_whitespace())
+    }
+
     pub fn push_inline_box(&mut self, mut inline_box: InlineBox) {
         if inline_box.kind == InlineBoxKind::InFlow {
             self.lcx.tree_style_builder.flush_pending_whitespace();
